(text "XO - 48 MHz  |  ECS-2520MV  |  ECS-2520MV-480-BN-TR  |  HCMOS clock oscillator" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 14.00 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f0d11dff-b44c-4386-a8b9-eaebb6054660"))
(text "House-common passives: 100 nF decoupling, 10k OE pull-up, 27R series termination." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 19.30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "21762c93-31e1-4a57-8821-b46e0fcc865a"))
(text "DESIGN EQUATIONS - 48 MHz XO, ECS-2520MV-480-BN-TR (ECS-2520MV datasheet)\nSupply: 1.6-3.6 V ; IDD max @3.3 V = 8 mA -> PDD = 26.4 mW ; standby (OE low) 10 uA\n  Decoupling: 100 nF X7R 0603 (house) within 2 mm of pin 4 ; add 1 uF bulk if the rail is shared with switching loads\nOutput: HCMOS, max load 15 pF ; rise/fall 7 ns max -> knee frequency 0.35/tr = 50 MHz\n  Load power C*V^2*f = 15 pF*3.3^2*48 MHz = 7.8 mW (included in IDD limit at full load)\nTermination: Rs = Z0 - Rout ~ 50 - (15..25) ohm -> 27R (house; same part as USB D+/D- series R)\n  Critical length (tr/6tpd, tpd ~6 ps/mm) = 194 mm ; keep fan-out to one load or use a clock buffer\nStability: +/-50 ppm all-inclusive (BN) -> +/-2400 Hz at 48 MHz ; USB needs +/-500 ppm (HS) - OK\nOE: pin 1 high or open = output active, low = Hi-Z ; 10k pull-up keeps it running when the OE net is unused.\nTypical use: USB 48 MHz ref" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 128.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left top)) (uuid "269847dc-e2ae-4465-be2b-0b7c3a33a513"))
